{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Recheck R-001 and compare other changed note and documentation claims against the selected code.","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R-001","severity":"medium","summary":"The revised readability claim still misses a separate home-file mask: known home `.env*` files are masked even when they are outside the named directories and files.","evidence":["The release notes and docs say a credential file outside the named directories and files stays readable.","In `task_run_claude_sandbox.py`, `sandbox_prefix` also masks every file found by `_credential_files(worktree)`. That helper additionally adds files matching `Path.home().glob(\".env*\")`, so a home credential such as `~/.env.production` is masked despite being outside `_SECRET_DIRECTORIES` and `_SECRET_FILES`.","The docs later acknowledge masks for known `.env*` files, which conflicts with the unqualified readability claim."] ,"action":"Qualify the claim to account for separately masked home `.env*` files, or include that exception in the stated mask list."},{"id":"R-002","severity":"high","summary":"The claim that real provider credentials stay in a parent-side proxy conflicts with the selected code’s OAuth-token fallback into the child environment.","evidence":["The release notes say provider credentials stay in a parent-side proxy; the docs say the child receives an invocation token.","In `configure_claude_environment`, when none of `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, or `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` is set, the code reads `~/.claude/.credentials.json` and assigns its `claudeAiOauth.accessToken` directly to `configured[\"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\"]`.","That fallback places the stored OAuth access token in the environment returned for the child, rather than keeping it solely in the proxy."] ,"action":"Reconcile the documentation with this fallback, or change the implementation so the child receives only a proxy invocation token."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Other reviewed sandbox-boundary statements","bin":"no additional concrete mismatch identified","disposition":"The supplied code supports the reviewed claims about the named directory/file masks, daemon socket paths, user runtime directory, network namespace flags, and the progress completion OSError handling."},{"concern":"Release-note test coverage and proxy implementation details","bin":"outside selected evidence","disposition":"No test files or proxy implementation source were supplied, so those claims were not independently verified."}],"next_move":"Correct the `.env*` readability exception and resolve the OAuth-token fallback claim, then recheck the revised sentences against the code.","non_claims":["Static review of the identity-checked semantic payload only; no tests or sandbox behavior were run.","The proxy implementation and test files were not among the selected inputs."]}
